; Cursor rules for projects using the Checkmarx One Go SDK (cxone-sdk-golang)

; --- Client Lifecycle ---
; Always construct the client with the builder: cxone.NewClient().Region(...).Tenant(...).AgentName(...).APIKey(...).Build()
; Always defer client.Close() immediately after Build() succeeds
; The client is safe to share across goroutines — create one, reuse it, close at shutdown
; Never use a client after Close()
; Required builder fields: Region (typed constant), Tenant, AgentName, and one of APIKey or OAuth

; --- Two-Layer Architecture ---
; Prefer the high-level workflow layer (client.Scans(), client.Projects(), client.Users(), client.Presets(), etc.)
; Use client.Advanced() only when the workflow layer does not cover the endpoint you need
; Both layers return strongly-typed models — never raw JSON or map[string]any

; --- Context & Cancellation ---
; Every SDK call takes context.Context as its first argument — always pass one
; Use context.WithTimeout for per-call timeouts (client default is 60s)
; Never use context.TODO() in production code

; --- Error Handling ---
; Use errors.As to discriminate SDK error types:
;   *cxerrors.ConfigurationError — bad config
;   *cxerrors.AuthError — token failed
;   *cxerrors.CommunicationError — retries exhausted / transport error
;   *cxerrors.ResponseError — unexpected status / unparseable body
;   *cxerrors.ScanError — scan workflow failure
;   *cxerrors.ReportError — report workflow failure
; Never swallow errors — they carry correlation IDs for server-side tracing

; --- Auth & Retry ---
; Auth is lazy — no token fetched until first API call
; 401 triggers automatic token refresh + one transparent retry (you don't handle this)
; SDK retries 3 times with randomized backoff on 5xx and transient errors
; Do NOT add your own retry wrapper around SDK calls

; --- Workflow Patterns ---
; Fluent builders for complex operations: client.Scans().NewScan(repo).ForBranch("main").WithEngines("sast").Start(ctx)
; Inspectors for state: insp.Executing(), insp.Successful(), insp.Failed(), insp.StateMessage()
; Waiters for polling: scans.WaitUntilComplete(ctx, insp, opts) — handles cancellation + terminal states
; Readers for cached catalogs: client.Presets(), client.Users().NewReader(), client.Roles().NewReader()
; Async factories for domain objects: wfprojects.FromProjectID(ctx, backend, id) — no I/O in constructors

; --- Observability ---
; Wire Logger/Metrics/Tracer via the builder — defaults are no-ops
; Structured events: request.start, request.end, request.retry, auth.refresh, scan.poll

; --- Models & Types ---
; Import models from github.com/cx-andrew-gehring/cxone-sdk-golang/models
; Use typed Region constants (cxone.RegionUS, cxone.RegionEU, etc.) — never hardcode URLs
; Unknown response fields are tolerated for forward compatibility

; --- Security ---
; The SDK redacts bearer tokens and secrets from all errors/logs/traces
; Never log credentials or circumvent the redaction

; --- Anti-Patterns ---
; Do NOT create a new client per request
; Do NOT add retry/backoff wrappers
; Do NOT parse raw HTTP responses — use typed models
; Do NOT hardcode Checkmarx One hostnames
; Do NOT ignore errors from client.Close()
